{
  "abstract": "A Lean formalization of the two main theorems of Chen, McDonald, and Shan. Theorem 1.3 proves the overfull criterion for sufficiently large robust expanders with linear maximum degree, weak Vizing adjacency, and few vertices of large degree deficit. Theorem 1.4 gives the criterion for sufficiently large simple graphs whose maximum degree is at least (1 + epsilon) times half the order, for every fixed positive epsilon. The proof includes the reduction to critical graphs, the two stopping routes, and the coloring of the canonical completion.",
